ui/gtk: side bar with phone buttons

sidebar=on puts a column of buttons next to the guest display: Home,
Lock, Volume + and Volume - (sent as F1, F2, F4 and F3, which ASoftware
iOS's kernel maps to the phone's buttons), Screenshot (a PNG in
Pictures/iOS Screenshots or $ASOFT_SHOTS_DIR), a button that opens that
folder, Install .ipa (copies the chosen files into $ASOFT_IPA_DIR, where
the guest fetches and installs them, and shows the result it leaves in
Installed/ or Failed/ there) and Shut down (power-down request; pressed
again, quit after asking). The buttons never take the keyboard focus.
Zoom-to-fit (0005) leaves room for the bar; full screen hides it. The
close button (0003) and Shut down share the power-down state.
Based on QEMU v11.1.2 with 0002-0005.

